      "dom_id": "question-18054",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14264040/assets/8927e58849984fbb42a7a3856e3b3509b9729b65031e066d29c6f94747ee5b6b.png)\n\nPoints $C$ and $D$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{CD}|.$",
      "worked_solution": "From the picture, we obtain $C(-3,4)$ and $D(2,3).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=-3i+4j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=2i+3j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =\\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC} \\\\  & =d-c \\\\  & =(2i+3j)-(-3i+4j) \\\\  & =5i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{CD}| & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{26}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
